        "answerKey": "Let r = x - y, s = y - z, t = z - x.\n1. u = f(r, s, t).\n2. By the Chain Rule:\n   du/dx = (du/dr)(dr/dx) + (du/ds)(ds/dx) + (du/dt)(dt/dx)\n         = (du/dr)(1) + (du/ds)(0) + (du/dt)(-1) = du/dr - du/dt\n   du/dy = (du/dr)(dr/dy) + (du/ds)(ds/dy) + (du/dt)(dt/dy)\n         = (du/dr)(-1) + (du/ds)(1) + (du/dt)(0) = -du/dr + du/ds\n   du/dz = (du/dr)(dr/dz) + (du/ds)(ds/dz) + (du/dt)(dt/dz)\n         = (du/dr)(0) + (du/ds)(-1) + (du/dt)(1) = -du/ds + du/dt\n3. Adding these equations:\n   du/dx + du/dy + du/dz = (du/dr - du/dt) + (-du/dr + du/ds) + (-du/ds + du/dt) = 0.\nHence proved."
