        "question": "Define orthogonal curvilinear coordinate systems. Find the scale factors $h_1, h_2, h_3$ for cylindrical coordinates $(\\rho, \\phi, z)$ and write the gradient $\\nabla\\psi$ in cylindrical coordinates.",
        "answerKey": "1. Curvilinear coords $(q_1,q_2,q_3)$ are orthogonal if the base vectors $\\mathbf{e}_i = \\frac{1}{h_i}\\frac{\\partial\\mathbf{r}}{\\partial q_i}$ are mutually perpendicular, where $h_i = |\\partial\\mathbf{r}/\\partial q_i|$ are scale factors.\n2. Cylindrical: $\\mathbf{r} = \\rho\\cos\\phi\\,\\hat{x}+\\rho\\sin\\phi\\,\\hat{y}+z\\,\\hat{z}$.\n3. $\\partial\\mathbf{r}/\\partial\\rho = (\\cos\\phi,\\sin\\phi,0)$, so $h_1 = h_\\rho = 1$.\n4. $\\partial\\mathbf{r}/\\partial\\phi = (-\\rho\\sin\\phi,\\rho\\cos\\phi,0)$, so $h_2 = h_\\phi = \\rho$.\n5. $\\partial\\mathbf{r}/\\partial z = (0,0,1)$, so $h_3 = h_z = 1$.\n6. Gradient: $\\nabla\\psi = \\frac{1}{h_\\rho}\\frac{\\partial\\psi}{\\partial\\rho}\\hat{e}_\\rho + \\frac{1}{h_\\phi}\\frac{\\partial\\psi}{\\partial\\phi}\\hat{e}_\\phi + \\frac{1}{h_z}\\frac{\\partial\\psi}{\\partial z}\\hat{e}_z = \\frac{\\partial\\psi}{\\partial\\rho}\\hat{e}_\\rho + \\frac{1}{\\rho}\\frac{\\partial\\psi}{\\partial\\phi}\\hat{e}_\\phi + \\frac{\\partial\\psi}{\\partial z}\\hat{e}_z$."
